                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "The Rogue Legacy comparison is unavoidable, but the vertical runs are short enough that you always get to something interesting fast, and the pacifist sigils genuinely changed how I approach levels once I realized skipping fights pays out too. Combat is on the shallow side, mostly about standing in the right spot and swinging, and by the time I was replaying Goblin Forest for the fifteenth time the repetition had set in. Still, the trait and ability rolls kept surprising me, teleporting a boss into lava never got old, and for the price it's an easy yes if you want something you can play in twenty minute chunks.",
